                <pb facs="0332" n="212" sameAs="frus:frus1905/pg212"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to Minister
                        Rockhill.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1905-08-12"><hi rendition="#italic">August 12,
                        1905</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Loomis informs Mr. Rockhill that the protests against the boycott filed in
                    the Department are increasing and are becoming more emphatic. Instructs him to
                    make a thorough investigation of the situation personally and through our
                    consuls, and to take as strong action as is deemed necessary.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
